    "title": "Boy dead following hit-and-run crash, two in custody - NewsBreak",
    "text": "WICHITA, Kan. (KSNW) — A boy believed to be between 10 and 14 years old was killed Wednesday evening in a hit-and-run crash in southeast Wichita. Wichita police said that officers were called to the intersection of Harry Street and Rock Road at 6:31 p.m. The boy was pronounced dead at the scene about 10 minutes later. Police said two suspects – a 24-year-old man and a 19-year-old man – ran from the vehicle that struck the boy. Both were located and taken into custody with help from the Kansas Highway Patrol. Investigators are still working to determine which of the two was driving at the time of the crash. The vehicle also struck a pole during the crash, which brought a power line down. The intersection remains closed as the investigation continues. No other suspects are being sought, police said. Police said the investigation is ongoing, and they do not yet know the identity of the boy struck and killed. For more Kansas news, click here . Keep up with the latest breaking news by downloading our mobile app and signing up for our news email alerts . Sign up for our Storm Track 3 Weather app by clicking here . To watch our shows live on our website, click here. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KSN-TV.",
